N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): the clip's 17 seconds were pitch-tracked between D4 and E6 with the steady crowd tone subtracted; the singing sits about 40 cents above A=440, and the long low note (7.9-9.3 s, sung with an octave below) is taken as the tonic F. Held notes from the track: C (0.7-1.0 s), A (4.0-4.7 s), the note between D and E flat (6.6-6.8 s), then F (7.9-9.3 s); a second phrase starts again high (9.5 s, A flat sliding down through G to F).
N:UNCERTAIN: almost everything: the F sharp at 5.9-6.2 s (a semitone above the tonic; perhaps F sung sharp, or a slide); the B heard at 1.2-1.4 s (a tritone above F, probably a slide from C, left out); whether the low passing note is D or E flat (it sits 250 cents below F); every length; the bar lines (the drum beat is a weak reading, about 0.30 s); which voice is the lead and which the seconds.
